# while loop skips an iteration through continue

Verifies `continue` abandons the current `while` iteration and re-evaluates
the condition, so the skipped value is never printed.

>>> source
let i: int = 0

while (i < 5) {
    i = i + 1

    if (i == 3) {
        continue
    }

    print(i)
}

<<< stdout
1
2
4
5

<<< stderr
